{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And open land</b> – an expanse, a smooth area outside the city all around, to serve as an adornment for the city. And they are not permitted to build a house in it, nor plant a vineyard, nor sow a crop — a thousand cubits all around (Numbers 35:4), and afterward it says two thousand cubits (Numbers 35:5). How so? He gives them two thousand all around, and of them the inner thousand are for the open land and the outer ones for fields all around and for vineyards — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 35:4) from the words of our Sages (Sotah 27). And the correct interpretation in my eyes according to the plain sense is that he is saying they shall give for the open land a thousand cubits in the surroundings of the city opposite it, so that its length shall be a thousand cubits, five hundred cubits in each direction, and its width likewise a thousand cubits, five hundred cubits in every direction. And afterward he said they shall make a square of two thousand cubits by two thousand cubits, and the city shall be in the middle of the square. He added to them open land not opposite the city in the same measure as the first portion that was opposite the city, until it turns out that when you leave for the open land a thousand cubits in its surroundings as was done at first, the city will be a thousand by a thousand in the square, and so the city is a quarter of what they give to the Levites. And know that the term פֵּאָה is used for an entire side, as in \"a hundred cubits in length for one פֵּאָה\" (Exodus 27:9) — for the entire side, and so all the occurrences mentioned there, and likewise the פֵּאוֹת at the end of the book of Ezekiel. Furthermore, if he had meant to measure from the city outward two thousand cubits in every direction, he would have said \"and you shall measure from outside the city to the side of the east\" and so on, but \"and you shall measure the side of the east\" is the measuring of that side as I have explained. And it is also fitting for their cities that they should have a square holding, not that they would measure two thousand cubits in the four directions opposite the city while the corners would not belong to them. And similar to this is \"all around eighteen thousand\" (Ezekiel 48:35), for the city among all its surroundings is eighteen thousand, for he counted in the four sides four thousand five hundred each, which are eighteen thousand altogether, for he measured in the four sides. And it is correct that the thousand cubits which he gave them all around opposite the city serve as open land that may not be sown, and the thousand which the second verse adds in the four sides are for fields and vineyards as our Sages received, but the name of the whole of it is מִגְרָשׁ in the language of Scripture, except that this one is worked and sown while that one is neither worked nor sown, and therefore Scripture distinguished the one from the other."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:10:28.673506459Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}